Cannot be established from this repository alone: the diff and surrounding context alone are not enough to say.
The mechanisms are visible, but the supplied diff does not establish runtime caller reachability, selected model/options, Google SDK retry configuration, or actual provider responses, so it cannot establish which real users or deployments observe them.

The Google chat adapter adds Gemini 2.5 model identifiers, changes how thinking configuration is sent, delegates retries to the Google client instead of performing its own retry loop, broadens structured-response parsing to accept fenced JSON, and adds detailed timing/error logging. Actual user impact depends on which callers instantiate this adapter, their options, provider responses, and Google SDK behavior.

Likely behavioral changes
  • Typed callers can now select three Gemini 2.5 model identifiers recognized by the adapter's verified-model annotation.
  • Invocations now default thinking_budget to 0, but every non-None value causes the provider request to receive a thinking budget of -1 rather than the configured value.
  • The adapter no longer performs its own ten-attempt exponential retry loop; it makes the call once at this layer and relies on retry behavior provided by the Google client.
  • When native structured output has no parsed object but returns JSON text enclosed in a complete Markdown code fence, the adapter now removes that fence before decoding and validating the JSON.
  • Google model calls now emit model-specific debug timing information and explicit warnings for empty text responses, changing operational observability without changing the returned empty-string fallback.

